MY CHEAT SHEET — FlockInsight
Last checked: 8 September 2026

The server changed on 4 September 2026. It no longer keeps one folder that you
update. It now downloads a fresh copy for each new version and keeps the last 5.
That is why "git pull" does not work any more.


=============================================================
1. LOG IN TO THE SERVER
=============================================================

ssh root@77.237.243.210

(I type the password myself.)


=============================================================
2. DEPLOY A NEW VERSION  — the only command I need
=============================================================

First, back up the database:

docker exec flockinsight-db pg_dump -U flockinsight -d flockinsight \
  | gzip > /root/flockinsight-$(date +%F-%H%M).sql.gz

Then deploy:

APP_ROOT=/home/flockinsight/app DEPLOY_BRANCH=main FLOCKINSIGHT_PORT=3005 \
  bash /home/flockinsight/app/current/deploy/deploy.sh

Copy the whole block. Takes a few minutes.
It finishes with:  ==> Deployed <code> — <the commit message>

This one command does everything: downloads the new code, installs packages,
updates the database, builds the site, tests the new version privately on a
spare port, and only then switches the live site over.

There is no separate build or restart step any more. Do not run "git pull",
"pnpm build" or "pm2 restart" by hand — they will fail or do nothing useful.

Why the two settings are needed:
  APP_ROOT       - without it the script looks in the wrong place
  DEPLOY_BRANCH  - my branch is "main"; the script expects "production"
  FLOCKINSIGHT_PORT - the site runs on port 3005


=============================================================
3. IF THE DEPLOY FAILS
=============================================================

I do not need to do anything. The script tests the new version before going
live. If it fails, the old version keeps running and nothing changes. If it
fails after going live, the script puts the old version back by itself.

To go back to an older version on purpose:

ls /home/flockinsight/app/releases          # newest is at the bottom
ln -sfn /home/flockinsight/app/releases/<the-one-I-want> /home/flockinsight/app/current
pm2 startOrReload /home/flockinsight/app/shared/ecosystem.config.cjs --update-env

Old versions are never deleted, only moved to releases/.trash/


=============================================================
4. SETTINGS AND PASSWORDS (env file)
=============================================================

One file, shared by every version:

/home/flockinsight/app/shared/.env

To add or change something:

nano /home/flockinsight/app/shared/.env

Then DEPLOY AGAIN (step 2). Restarting alone will not pick up the change.


=============================================================
5. MAKE SOMEONE A SUPER ADMIN
=============================================================

docker exec flockinsight-db psql -U flockinsight -d flockinsight \
  -c "UPDATE \"user\" SET is_super_admin=true WHERE email='THE_EMAIL_HERE';"


=============================================================
6. QUICK CHECKS
=============================================================

pm2 list                    # is the site running? (2 workers named flockinsight)
pm2 logs flockinsight       # see errors as they happen (Ctrl+C to stop)
curl -s localhost:3005/api/health    # shows which version is live

If the site looks broken or unstyled after a deploy, purge the Cloudflare cache.


=============================================================
7. THE ROADMAP
=============================================================

Where I add features I want built: flockinsight.com/superadmin/roadmap

Claude reads it here (needs the key from shared/.env):

curl -H "Authorization: Bearer MY_ROADMAP_KEY" https://flockinsight.com/api/roadmap

Without the key, that address only shows the features I ticked as "public".


=============================================================
8. THINGS I MUST NEVER LOSE
=============================================================

  - /home/flockinsight/app/shared/.env        (all the site's passwords)
  - /root/.flockinsight-backup.key            (unlocks the database backups)
  - My GitHub login                            (all the code lives there)
  - My Contabo login                           (the server itself)
  - My Cloudflare login                        (the domain)

Keep copies of these in a password manager, not only on this laptop.
Database backups run every night at 02:00 and also copy to Google Drive.
